                "**Agree the boundaries** for both measures and write them down as a policy, as above.",
                "**Record three or four dates on every card:** requested, started, finished and, if different, delivered. Digital tools log these from status changes; on a physical board, write them on the card. Our [Kanban cards](/project-management/kanban/kanban-cards/) guide shows a layout.",
                "**Wait until items are finished.** Lead time and cycle time are measured on completed work. For items still in progress, track work item age instead.",
                "**Calculate per item** in a spreadsheet: one column for lead time, one for cycle time and, usefully, one for queue time before start (start date − request date).",
                "**Summarise the distribution** with the median and 85th percentile for each measure, not just the average.",
                "**Compare the two medians.** The gap is the typical waiting time before and after work, and it tells you where to look first.",
