            "Two cautions. First, Little's Law describes averages in a reasonably stable system, where work arrives at about the rate it leaves and items that start eventually finish; use it to understand cause and effect, not to forecast a single item. Second, an uncommitted backlog of ideas is not a queue: many options will be discarded or replaced, so counting them as WIP overstates lead time. Apply the law from the commitment point, or from the request if every request will be done.",
